    "0b6e5731-d184-5908-bc56-490b0fb25ab5": {
      "id": "0b6e5731-d184-5908-bc56-490b0fb25ab5",
      "title": "Phase 1",
      "sectionId": "a12dbb63-6411-59c3-8425-aed7df48eef2",
      "isIntro": false,
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "a8f246f1-6541-53c8-998d-b73ebce69a27",
          "title": "Phase 1",
          "required": true,
          "done": false,
          "video": null,
          "poster": null,
          "clips": [],
          "body": "![](/media/ext/d11n7da8rpqbjy/mikesalemi/29554765_1658532062MwiEbook_Sample_Cover_and_Body_Designs.png)\n\nIn this phase, you develop what I call body integrity. Body integrity is the ability to feel where your body is in space and maintain safe positions throughout the exercise. In other words, it's the foundation.\n\n**Skills**\n\n- Postural awareness\n- Breathing Bodyweight control\n- Grips Positions Warmups/cool downs\n- Training barefoot\n\n**Movements**\n\n- Goblet Squat\n- Deadlift\n- Half Kneeling Overhead Press OR Halo (if mobility doesn’t allow for quality overhead movements)\n- Single Arm Row\n\n**Benchmarks**\n\n- 20 spinal roll ups\n- Glute bridges 30 without feeling it in your back\n- 30 bodyweight squats\n- For the 4 KB movements: 15 reps with a light KB hitting the standards of quality, *reuse the material from KBL + add in quantity, be able to stay nasal breathing during 15-20 min walk/30 squats/easy workout",
          "description": null,
          "attachments": []
        }
      ],
      "videoSeconds": {}
    }
